  "reason": "R1 establishes that an MTP can achieve near-DFT fidelity in the closely related BCC refractory NbMoTaW system, providing strong support for the central structural mediator, while R16 identifies the relevant weakness of EAM potentials at elevated temperature. R2 supports SRO as an energetically important contribution in a closely related refractory alloy, and R12, R13, R17, and R18 show that electronic or magnetic free-energy terms and DOS features can shift calculated phase stability. However, none of the records proposes training a liquid-phase MTP for TaVCrW, using the small MTP–DFT energy-difference variance to enable FEP, or replacing TI with FEP. Thus, the literature points toward a high-fidelity ML potential and omitted free-energy contributions, but the integrated MTP–FEP melting workflow still requires a substantial new idea."
